    "body": "## 1. Overview\r\n\r\nThis PR adds optimized **SM90 MXFP4 MegaMoE** to `nv_dev`. Derived from [#440](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/pull/440), with MXFP4 format and decoder foundations from [#411](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepGEMM/pull/411) (referencing Humming). Our additions include tiled register decoding, specialized small-M buckets, direct swap epilogues, MXFP4 split-M and tail optimization, and optional single-token split-K.\r\n\r\nEP8 speedups across M=1--8192:\r\n\r\n| EP8 shape | vs #383 FP8 | vs #440 FP8 | vs #411 MXFP4 |\r\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| Flash | 1.08--1.52x | 1.08--2.04x | 1.10--1.44x |\r\n| Pro | 1.12--1.48x | 1.32--1.89x | 1.11--1.44x |\r\n\r\n## 2. Two key optimizations\r\n\r\n- **Small M: tiled register decoding + RS WGMMA.** Pack each 256-row x K128 weight stage into a contiguous 16 KiB tile and decode directly into register A fragments, avoiding expanded-weight shared-memory traffic and associated synchronization. Extend #411's swapAB with N8/16/24/32/40/48 buckets, selected double buffering, and direct SwiGLU/quantization epilogues.\r\n\r\n- **Large M and tails: MXFP4 split-M.** Use 128x256 tiles with two math warpgroups sharing decoded weights; specialize partial tiles with RS buckets, a dual N96 swap path, and empty-half WGMMA skipping. Order dynamic tails by valid rows and preserve the scaling chain for bitwise repeatability.\r\n\r\n## 3. Performance against #411, #383, and #440: M=1--8192\r\n\r\n- **Hardware:** H20-3e, 78 SMs/GPU, CUDA 13, PyTorch 2.13.0+cu130.\r\n- **Precision:** FP8 activations; FP8 weights for #383/#440, MXFP4 weights for #411/this PR; common source weights, routing, FP8 inputs, and fixed RNE MXFP4 quantization.\r\n- **Timing:** CUDA Graph, seed0, 3 interleaved rounds x 50 samples.\r\n- **Speedup:** baseline latency / this PR latency.\r\n\r\n### EP8, Flash\r\n\r\n(hidden=4096, intermediate=2048, experts/GPU=32, top-k=6) (us)\r\n\r\n| M | #383 FP8 | #440 FP8 | #411 MXFP4 | This PR MXFP4 | Speedup vs #411 |\r\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| 1 | 50.2 | 88.9 | 66.8 | **46.4** | 1.44x |\r\n| 2 | 63.8 | 89.6 | 67.5 | **53.0** | 1.27x |\r\n| 4 | 83.3 | 127.6 | 92.5 | **69.1** | 1.34x |\r\n| 8 | 102.7 | 148.8 | 106.2 | **78.8** | 1.35x |\r\n| 16 | 151.7 | 227.1 | 159.4 | **117.0** | 1.36x |\r\n| 32 | 196.1 | 300.9 | 202.5 | **151.5** | 1.34x |\r\n| 64 | 219.1 | 340.6 | 227.0 | **169.2** | 1.34x |\r\n| 128 | 270.0 | 420.4 | 276.4 | **206.3** | 1.34x |\r\n| 256 | 282.0 | 423.8 | 290.4 | **211.3** | 1.37x |\r\n| 512 | 321.9 | 427.2 | 313.7 | **233.0** | 1.35x |\r\n| 1024 | 412.0 | 429.1 | 376.8 | **270.2** | 1.39x |\r\n| 2048 | 467.6 | 454.8 | 456.2 | **410.7** | 1.11x |\r\n| 4096 | 880.6 | 800.1 | 840.3 | **739.1** | 1.14x |\r\n| 8192 | 1485.5 | 1549.4 | 1445.0 | **1316.9** | 1.10x |\r\n\r\n### EP8, Pro\r\n\r\n(hidden=7168, intermediate=3072, experts/GPU=48, top-k=6) (us)\r\n\r\n| M | #383 FP8 | #440 FP8 | #411 MXFP4 | This PR MXFP4 | Speedup vs #411 |\r\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| 1 | 98.3 | 122.6 | 98.3 | **83.9** | 1.17x |\r\n| 2 | 110.9 | 152.7 | 114.0 | **99.1** | 1.15x |\r\n| 4 | 133.1 | 191.4 | 135.1 | **117.0** | 1.15x |\r\n| 8 | 230.3 | 316.6 | 213.5 | **184.8** | 1.16x |\r\n| 16 | 346.1 | 505.6 | 323.5 | **280.9** | 1.15x |\r\n| 32 | 507.3 | 782.8 | 482.5 | **424.5** | 1.14x |\r\n| 64 | 693.4 | 1065.2 | 642.5 | **568.2** | 1.13x |\r\n| 128 | 957.8 | 1476.5 | 897.3 | **782.2** | 1.15x |\r\n| 256 | 1024.6 | 1523.1 | 957.1 | **806.7** | 1.19x |\r\n| 512 | 1065.8 | 1530.3 | 989.2 | **832.7** | 1.19x |\r\n| 1024 | 1203.1 | 1539.4 | 1125.4 | **899.7** | 1.25x |\r\n| 2048 | 1603.6 | 1555.3 | 1560.4 | **1085.0** | 1.44x |\r\n| 4096 | 2475.8 | 2964.8 | 2441.8 | **2060.5** | 1.19x |\r\n| 8192 | 3915.4 | 4511.0 | 3803.5 | **3425.6** | 1.11x |\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Single-GPU results: M=1--8192</summary>\r\n\r\n- M = total active tokens; cap = max(128, align(M,128)); split-K disabled.\r\n- Flash/Pro run on separate GPUs, with the same GPU for all variants of each shape.\r\n\r\n### Single GPU, Flash\r\n\r\n(hidden=4096, intermediate=2048, experts/GPU=32, top-k=6) (us)\r\n\r\n| M | #383 FP8 | #440 FP8 | #411 MXFP4 | This PR MXFP4 | Speedup vs #411 |\r\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| 1 | 79.0 | 118.1 | 79.5 | **66.2** | 1.20x |\r\n| 2 | 115.1 | 158.5 | 110.6 | **84.0** | 1.32x |\r\n| 4 | 166.0 | 250.4 | 155.4 | **124.4** | 1.25x |\r\n| 8 | 218.8 | 330.9 | 211.5 | **160.8** | 1.32x |\r\n| 16 | 253.1 | 402.7 | 241.2 | **190.2** | 1.27x |\r\n| 32 | 274.5 | 407.3 | 266.7 | **196.8** | 1.36x |\r\n| 64 | 312.1 | 410.2 | 292.8 | **215.2** | 1.36x |\r\n| 128 | 387.1 | 412.0 | 341.9 | **247.6** | 1.38x |\r\n| 256 | 451.1 | 422.0 | 427.2 | **377.9** | 1.13x |\r\n| 512 | 854.5 | 776.6 | 826.1 | **699.4** | 1.18x |\r\n| 1024 | 1399.6 | 1506.0 | 1375.7 | **1268.4** | 1.08x |\r\n| 2048 | 2575.2 | 2539.8 | 2504.3 | **2339.9** | 1.07x |\r\n| 4096 | 4939.7 | 4874.9 | 4861.2 | **4584.8** | 1.06x |\r\n| 8192 | 9625.7 | 9328.1 | 9575.6 | **9050.8** | 1.06x |\r\n\r\n### Single GPU, Pro\r\n\r\n(hidden=7168, intermediate=3072, experts/GPU=48, top-k=6) (us)\r\n\r\n| M | #383 FP8 | #440 FP8 | #411 MXFP4 | This PR MXFP4 | Speedup vs #411 |\r\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| 1 | 163.7 | 215.7 | 140.8 | **111.5** | 1.26x |\r\n| 2 | 251.7 | 375.9 | 237.4 | **176.8** | 1.34x |\r\n| 4 | 433.5 | 646.9 | 392.0 | **291.1** | 1.35x |\r\n| 8 | 646.7 | 985.1 | 585.5 | **428.9** | 1.37x |\r\n| 16 | 850.5 | 1308.9 | 788.0 | **563.3** | 1.40x |\r\n| 32 | 979.0 | 1496.5 | 921.9 | **643.6** | 1.43x |\r\n| 64 | 1017.5 | 1502.2 | 955.0 | **668.7** | 1.43x |\r\n| 128 | 1132.3 | 1510.2 | 1092.7 | **754.9** | 1.45x |\r\n| 256 | 1571.6 | 1528.2 | 1540.4 | **945.7** | 1.63x |\r\n| 512 | 2348.3 | 2888.3 | 2280.1 | **1951.5** | 1.17x |\r\n| 1024 | 3773.1 | 4337.0 | 3704.7 | **3482.8** | 1.06x |\r\n| 2048 | 6756.4 | 7086.2 | 6630.1 | **6216.6** | 1.07x |\r\n| 4096 | 12725.8 | 12860.9 | 12596.9 | **11960.8** | 1.05x |\r\n| 8192 | 24868.9 | 24766.9 | 24639.8 | **23700.7** | 1.04x |\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Validation and reproduction</summary>\r\n\r\n- **Correctness:** single-GPU/EP8 reference and repeatability checks pass (MXFP4 tolerance 0.002; FP8 0.01); 96 per-rank outputs match the accepted pre-port implementation bitwise.\r\n- **SASS:** six FP8 checks unchanged; 30 measured MXFP4 cubins have STACK <=16 B and no CALL.ABS.\r\n- **Reproduction:** frozen commits, commands, maximum-rank timings, and per-round data are in `docs/sm90-fused-mxfp4-benchmarks.md` and `docs/benchmarks/sm90-fused-mxfp4-h20.csv`.\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## 4. Follow-up work\r\n\r\n- **Shared experts:** integrate and benchmark overlap with routed experts.\r\n- **vLLM:** validate the upstream implementation and measure end-to-end latency and throughput.\r\n- **Scheduler:** improve dispatch/compute overlap, load balancing, and tail scheduling.\r\n- **H100/H200:** validate correctness and performance and tune hardware-specific heuristics.",
